> Actual saved attention layout

This reads `outputs.npz`, field `cross_attention`, from the real held-out run. It shows the first leading-index slice and at most64 rows/columns. For sparse, hashed or projected attention, candidate slots are the source layout, not a dense physical-token axis. The complete program retains the index/projection mappings. Attention is not a saliency or causal explanation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/transformer_nmt_attention.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto load=[](const std::string&path){auto a=dm::nn::load_npz(path);return std::map<std::string,dm::nn::Tensor>(a.begin(),a.end());};auto a=load("build/nn-completion/models/transformer_nmt/outputs.npz");auto tensor=a.at("cross_attention");int rows=tensor.size(tensor.dim()-2),columns=tensor.size(tensor.dim()-1),r=std::min(rows,64),c=std::min(columns,64);auto values=tensor.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x(c),y(r);std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);std::iota(y.begin(),y.end(),0.);std::vector<std::vector<double>>z(c,std::vector<double>(r));for(int i=0;i<r;++i)for(int j=0;j<c;++j)z[j][i]=values[i*columns+j];std::print("Native saved cross_attention last axes: {} by {}; showing first sample/head/chunk and up to64 positions. Colour range: zero to the maximum in these rows, {}.\n",rows,columns,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.begin()+r*columns));dm::graphics::RPlot::create().image(x,y,z,dm::graphics::terrain_colors(256),0,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.begin()+r*columns)).title("transformer nmt actual cross_attention").x_label("Source key/candidate/compressed slot index").y_label("Source query/layout row index").size(1000,750).save_svg("build/transformer_nmt_attention.svg");}
